-
-## Mods and shader packs
-
-- **Content mods** (`.hmod`): blocks, items, recipes, loot, models and textures, with no code.
-- **Native mods** (`.hnmod`): Rust that the launcher compiles into the game for you, with nothing to install.
-- **Java mods** (Fabric, NeoForge, Forge) don't run: Horizon has no Java. The launcher carries over the data and assets inside their jars, and imports modpacks (`.mrpack`, CurseForge zips, Prism instances) the same way ([modpacks](https://playhorizon.dev/docs/modpacks)).
-- **Shader packs**: Iris/OptiFine-format packs (`shaders/` folders) and Horizon's own WGSL packs, under Video Settings → Shader Packs ([pack format](docs/shaders.md)).
-
-Mods are off by default: a fresh install plays exactly like vanilla 26.3. The launcher's Mods page browses Horizon's registry and Modrinth. [Mods](https://playhorizon.dev/docs/mods) · [make a mod](docs/mods.md).
-
-## Host a server
-
-The launcher's **Servers** page creates, starts, backs up and updates a server, and invites friends. On a VPS, `horizon-server` installs with one command, needs no Java, and takes vanilla 26.3 and Horizon players alike. [Host a server](https://playhorizon.dev/docs/hosting) ([reference](docs/hosting.md)).
-
-## Agent control
-
-AI agents and scripts can play Horizon. `horizon-ctl`, shipped with the game, reads its state as JSON and acts like a player; `horizon-ctl mcp` serves the same commands over MCP.
-
-```sh
-horizon-ctl launch --world Survival --seed 5 --wait   # finds the version the launcher installed
-horizon-ctl state                                       # position, health, food, target, screen...
-horizon-ctl goto -0.5 65 -2.5 --near 2.5                # walks there along a path
-horizon-ctl break -1 65 -3                              # mines it; replies with the drops
-```
-
-`horizon-ctl help` lists every command. [Agent control](docs/native-client.md#agent-control-horizon-ctl-and-mcp).
-
-## Build from source
-
-Needs Rust 1.90+, Python 3.10+, JDK 25, and on Linux `libasound2-dev libudev-dev`. `horizon-prepare` builds the game's resources from **your own copy** of Java Edition 26.3 (checked against `research-lock.json`) and never downloads it:
-
-1. **Client:** play 26.3 once in the official launcher. Horizon reads `~/.minecraft` (or `--minecraft-dir` / `HORIZON_MINECRAFT_DIR`).
-2. **Server jar:** the 26.3 server jar (`downloads.server.url` in `versions/26.3/26.3.json`), passed once with `--server-jar` or `HORIZON_SERVER_JAR`.
-
-```sh
-git clone https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon.git
-cd horizon
-cargo run --release -p horizon-prepare -- --prepare --server-jar ~/Downloads/server.jar   # needs JDK 25
-cargo run --release -p horizon-prepare -- sounds   # optional: sounds from your launcher install
-cargo run --release -p horizon-client
-```
-
-Prepared files land in the gitignored `.local/`: never commit or share them. Options, controls and architecture: [the native client guide](docs/native-client.md); all developer docs: [docs/README.md](docs/README.md).
+<p align="center"><b>Horizon iOS</b><br>
+<sub>A native iPhone and iPad port of Horizon, the Minecraft: Java Edition 26.3 rewrite in Rust.</sub></p>
+
+> **Unofficial project.** Horizon iOS is not an official Minecraft product, is not approved by or
+> associated with Mojang or Microsoft, and is not affiliated with the Horizon project or its
+> maintainers. Minecraft is a trademark of Mojang Synergies AB. You must own Minecraft: Java
+> Edition 26.3 to prepare and use the game data.
+
+**Status: `v0.1.0-experimental`.** This is a first public experimental release for developers and
+experienced sideloaders. It is **not** on the App Store, has no notarized build, and ships **no
+Minecraft code or assets**. There is no launcher and no Microsoft sign-in. See
+[RELEASE_NOTES.md](RELEASE_NOTES.md) for artifacts, checksums and the verification record.
+
+## What it is
+
+Horizon iOS embeds the real Horizon client — gameplay, world generation, an integrated server,
+multiplayer, saves and the vanilla UI — in a native iOS app. Rendering uses `wgpu` on Metal, the
+window and lifecycle use `winit` on UIKit, and touch input and the keyboard are bridged into
+Horizon's existing actions. There is no Java runtime, no JIT, no interpreter and no jailbreak
+requirement.
+
+The port lives in [`ios/`](ios/) (UIKit host and Xcode project) and
+[`crates/horizon-ios/`](crates/horizon-ios/) (Rust entry point, resource import, lifecycle,
+diagnostic scenes). Gameplay fixes belong upstream; this repository carries only the platform
+integration.
+
+## What works
+
+- **Single player.** A Creative world backed by Horizon's integrated server, with the real
+  Overworld generator, lighting, meshing, block breaking and placement, inventory and saving.
+- **Multiplayer.** Direct address entry, login and play against compatible Java servers. Online-mode
+  authentication has not been validated on iOS; use servers that accept offline profiles unless
+  you have tested your setup.
+- **Touch controls.** Left-thumb movement, right-hand look, jump, break, place, pick block,
+  inventory, pause and chat. Back follows the current screen's own cancellation semantics.
+- **Native text input.** The iOS keyboard edits Horizon's own fields, including server addresses
+  (IPv4, IPv6 and explicit ports), chat, signs, books and dialogs.
+- **Streaming.** Chunk generation, lighting, meshing and upload on Horizon's existing workers, with
+  a small first-launch render distance that can be raised in Video Settings.
+- **Persistence.** Saves in the app sandbox, plus a bounded background save when the app is
+  backgrounded.
+- **Resource import.** The app verifies a content-addressed copy of your own prepared 26.3 files
+  before opening a world. Corrupt or missing files are reported instead of silently loading.
+
+## Tested hardware
+
+These are the devices used by the port's maintainers. Other arm64 devices on iOS 16 or later may
+work, but are untested.
+
+| Device | SoC | OS | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| iPhone 13 mini | A15 | iOS 27.2 | Release builds; integrated gameplay, touch controls, native keyboard, background save and relaunch |
+| iPad 5 (`iPad6,11`) | A9, 2 GB RAM | iPadOS 16.7.16 | Older validation build; about 60 FPS in normal play and 40–50 FPS while generating chunks, at 50% render resolution and a 10-chunk setting. Those are user observations, not controlled benchmarks |
+| iPhone 17 Pro simulator | Apple silicon host | iOS 27.0 | Automated UI and gameplay checks |
+
+The current tree's first-launch defaults are more conservative than the iPad figures above: render
+distance 2, simulation distance 5, 60 FPS cap. Raise them in Video Settings on hardware that can
+afford it. Long sessions, thermals, memory pressure on 2 GB devices and modified-block persistence
+after a device save/relaunch still need more validation. See [KNOWN_ISSUES.md](KNOWN_ISSUES.md).
+
+## Requirements
+
+- An arm64 iPhone or iPad on **iOS/iPadOS 16.0 or later**.
+- A legally owned **Minecraft: Java Edition 26.3** installation on a Mac, used to prepare your own
+  resource files. The app never downloads Minecraft and this repository never contains its data.
+- To build: an Apple silicon Mac with a full Xcode installation and Rust. See
+  [BUILDING.md](BUILDING.md).
+- To install an unsigned IPA: a re-signing tool that accepts your Apple ID or development team
+  (Sideloadly, AltStore, Xcode, or a paid developer account). Free Apple ID signatures expire after
+  seven days.
+
+## Install
+
+1. **Build or obtain an app.** Build from source with [BUILDING.md](BUILDING.md), or re-sign the
+   unsigned IPA as described in [INSTALL.md](INSTALL.md).
+2. **Prepare your own resources** on the Mac and copy the resulting `HorizonResources` folder into
+   the app's Documents folder (Finder → device → Files → Horizon iOS, or the Files app).
+3. **Launch the app.** It verifies the import, then opens the bundled Creative world. The first
+   import can take a while; a progress message is shown.
+
+The full walkthrough, including signing, installing and updating, is in [INSTALL.md](INSTALL.md).
+Exact build commands are in [BUILDING.md](BUILDING.md).
+
+## Known limitations
+
+- No App Store distribution, launcher, Microsoft sign-in, audio output, controller support, Realms
+  or mod installation.
+- Online-mode servers and simultaneous physical multiplayer have not been fully validated.
+- Some older GrimAC/PacketEvents builds kick 26.3 clients when several players join. This was
+  reproduced with vanilla clients and is a server-side plugin compatibility problem; see
+  [KNOWN_ISSUES.md](KNOWN_ISSUES.md).
+- Performance varies by device. No thermal, long-run or controlled frame-time study exists yet.
